            "createdOn": 1757370671,
            "author": {
                "name": "rcheng123",
                "email": "rocheng@nvidia.com",
                "username": "rcheng123"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you note which specific eeprom chip has this issue you are fixing here, that `i2c_smbus_write_byte_data` does not work."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "+1.  Also how it fails and why it doesn't work."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "rcheng123",
                        "email": "rocheng@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "rcheng123"
                    },
                    "message": "@alexander.hansen@9elements.com @spinler@us.ibm.com this is for 24AA64. Given it's 64kibit EEPROM looks like you need to pass in a 2-byte address (higher and lower order bytes) [1] which smbus commands does not support [2].\n\n[1] 24AA64 data sheet -> see section 6.0 WRITE OPERATIONS: https://ww1.microchip.com/downloads/aemDocuments/documents/MPD/ProductDocuments/DataSheets/24AA64-24FC64-24LC64-64-Kbit-I2C-Serial-EEPROM-DS20001189.pdf\n\n[2] https://docs.kernel.org/i2c/smbus-protocol.html -> command bytes is only 8 bits"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Nice, thanks for the explanation \ud83d\udc4d, can you kindly add it to the commit message for future reference?\n\n\nDo you think your code will work as well for eeproms accepting a 1-byte address?\n\nOtherwise, does it make sense to make a separate function to handle things differently depending on which eeprom is used."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "rcheng123",
                        "email": "rocheng@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "rcheng123"
                    },
                    "message": "You're right. The ioctl command writes both higher and lower byte which may not work with 8-bit address.\n\nUpdated the code to check if device is 16 or 8 bits. Then calls ioctl or smbus commands respectively.\n\nUpdated my commit message."
                }
            ],
